figdown 0.1 block
# 0.1: `title` takes exactly ONE quoted string. The unquoted
# rest-of-line form is retired — it was the only directive that accepted an
# unquoted string containing spaces (`node`, `class`, `group` and `boundary`
# all report `unexpected argument "..."`), and it carried three defects.
title TCP Header
# (1) a title could never contain a `#`: the comment scanner cut the line, so
# this used to yield "A", never "A # note".
title A # note
# (2) inner quotes escaped into the value: this used to yield `A B C`.
title A "B" C
# (3) escapes resolved ONLY in the quoted form, so the same visible text gave
# different values depending on quoting — a literal backslash-n here, a real
# newline in `title "A\nB"`.
title A\nB
# one quoted string, and nothing after it
title "TCP Header" extra
node a "A"
